{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1502196583,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNDg3MDQwMzA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1691","origin":"github"},"title":"Nipype example failing","message":"As mentioned in PR #1690, I looked into the failure of the nipype example.\nWhat is failing is the `datalad publish -r` command, called from within the modified superdataset from `datasets.datalad.org`. We added a new subdataset and want to publish the entire beast. The issue here is, that we didn't install all the other subdatasets of `///`. Actually it's working (meaning: it publishes what is  expected), but returns non-zero, since the recursive publishing of the superdataset yields `impossible` for all the not installed subdatasets.\nWe have no nice and obvious way to avoid that. `datalad publish` itself provides a `--missing=skip` option, but this one is for missing siblings to publish to, not for locally absent subdatasets. I guess we need an additional option here. Do you agree, @datalad/developers ?\n\nAn ugly approach to make the test pass would be to use `--on-failure=ignore`, but this is bad for a test, since we can't specify the failure we want to ignore. Furthermore it doesn't work in this case.","files":null}]}